# ★personal data — this never goes into the repository★
#
# This tool gets installed and used by many people, each on their own computer. The files below are
# ★that person's own★ and must not be shared. Scoring against someone else's gold makes it impossible
# to tell whether a failure is the engine or a different corpus, and config's paths are that person's own folder layout.

# install.sh detects and builds this per environment (config.example.json is the template)
config.json

# eval set — the queries come from your own conversation history and gold is your own memory names.
# build your own set with `bin/brain eval-init`. Only the format examples are shared.
#
# ⛔⛔ ★don't block this by extension — on 2026-09-03, `short.json.bak` slipped past that rule and
#      14KB (90 real queries + 34 gold) stayed ★tracked★.★ Backup and temp copies show up
#      under any extension. So ★the whole folder is blocked and only the examples are opened★.
#   ⛔ And `.gitignore` only ignores ★untracked★ files — anything already added keeps following
#      you even after the rule is fixed (`git rm --cached` is required).
tests/eval/*
!tests/eval/*.example.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# local artifacts
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# packaging artifacts — ★never goes into the repository★ (leftovers here poison the next install with stale package-data)
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# the ★internal-name list★ the scrub check looks for — if this file goes into the repository,
# the checker itself becomes a leak (the thing it searches for ends up carrying it). Everyone builds their own.
tests/scrub_terms.txt
